  "security_implications": "The chunk aggregates multiple error and fault conditions (invalid_op_i, disabled_i, invalid_i, kmac_input_invalid_i, fault_o) during an operation update/done window (err_vld). The assertion of sync_err_d[SyncErrInvalidOp] when any fault_o bit is high can directly trigger a wipe sequence in the key manager, protecting secret key material from being used or exposed in a corrupted state. A missed error due to a glitch or incorrect gating could allow a faulty operation to proceed, while a false error could unnecessarily wipe secrets and cause denial-of-service. Therefore the correctness and glitch-free behavior of these assignment expressions is security-critical.",
